ormers.\n- **Debt:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably, so stronger issuers can borrow.\n- **Equity:** Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short. Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size. Utilities can't rely on this route.\n- **Pellham:** It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves. That suggests debt alone could not close its funding gap.\n- **Norvane:** It looks able to fund its smaller increase through bonds. I only have the one C$1.1B deal to go on, so I can't say whether it covers the whole plan.\n\nThe sources don't give total funding needs, leverage, credit ratings or Norvane's equity needs. So I can't say how much debt capacity Pellham has left. I also can't say whether Pellham could have issued bonds instead of cutting spending.\n\nPellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, so its cuts could reduce equipment demand across the country.\n\nThe debt and equity findings come from child nodes n5 and n6. Both drew on the documents `utility-capex-2027`, `utility-credit` and `pellham-offering`.","ttft_ms":2041,"type":"result","duration_ms":26890,"uuid":"07f5d8f6-c6e9-4317-a68a-0b9f701c38cf","ttft_stream_ms":1807,"time_to_request_ms":496,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":46,"system_prompt":22,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":12,"input_attachments":74,"input_hooks":24,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":44,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":39,"init_frame_send":25,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":19,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":75,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":7,"tool_schema_build":14,"message_normalization":13,"client_creation":14,"request_build":63},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":274,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":89,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"